<?xml version="1.0"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="TROME">
    <!--
     A walk into and out of the 150 m area of Le Parc de Saint-Maur (RER A), in 5 min 50 s,
     to see the area lines of the Wake log on an iPhone at your desk.
     It starts 600 m north and waits 20 s, comes to 15 m of the station, stays inside the area
     for about 2 min 30 s, leaves to 450 m south, and waits there.
     Every other station of the app stays more than 1 km away.

     1. Run the app on the iPhone from Xcode, with the real GPS and the location set to Always.
     2. Xcode: Debug > Simulate Location > WalkIntoLeParcDeSaintMaur.
     3. App: Testing tools > Wake log.
        Within about 3 minutes: "iOS: entered Le Parc de Saint-Maur (phone N m away, ...)".
        Within about 6 minutes: "iOS: left Le Parc de Saint-Maur (phone N m away, ...)".
     4. Xcode: Debug > Simulate Location > Don't Simulate Location. App: Clear. Xcode: Stop.

     Xcode moves the phone until you pick Don't Simulate Location.
     -->
    <wpt lat="48.810806" lon="2.486624">
        <time>2026-10-18T12:00:00Z</time>
    </wpt>
    <wpt lat="48.810806" lon="2.486624">
